15. Bxc4 Qxc4 16. Rad1 a5 17. Qd3 b5 {Source: Aitken Book 43. "Slagboom's
round 3 game against Tunc Alankus from Turkey turned into a dead-drawn endgame.
As the evening drew on, Slagboom became so frustrated when his offers of a
draw were turned down that, after 10 hours' play in one day, he blundered and
lost; swept the pieces off the board and withdrew from the tournament." (CHESS,
November 1980, Vol.45, No.s 845-6, p319). Bulletin crosstable shows Black's
initial to be 'T'. He was a Dutch player.} 1/2-1/2

